import UnforcedLeray.Short.PartIIb.Sub.PartIIb_S3_1_1_2

/-!
# Comoving phase-derivative tower (`PartII-b:S3/1/1/2`, `PartII-b:S3/1/1/2/1`, `PartII-b:S3/1/2`)

Source of record: `the November 2 reference manuscript`
(SP), lines 2519-2523 ("The projected equation is $A_0U+\mathbb P(U\cdot\nabla U)=0$ with zero
residual") and 2559-2562 ("On positive physical-time compact intervals the resulting
$C_\tau W^{k,4}$ regularity and the projected equation give all time derivatives, so $U$ is
jointly smooth through the axis").

The maximal graph `B0411.D p.period p.ν q0E` (`Units/B0411.lean`, `mem_D`) controls `u`, `νΔu` and
the comoving derivative `T₀u = (∂_τ - ½ y·∇)u` in `Y_q`, not `∂_τ u` or `(y·∇)u` separately. Time
derivatives are therefore taken along the comoving rays `t ↦ (τ + t, e^{-t/2} y)` generated by `T₀`,
on which the physical position `x = e^{τ/2} y` is fixed (`HasComovingJetDeriv`,
`JointSmoothSub.comovingPullback`, `Sub/PartII-b_S3_1.lean`). Along these rays the projected
equation reads `T₀U = νΔU + ½U - 𝔓(U·∇U)` (`comovingEvolRHS`), with no radial-drift term, and `T₀`
commutes with `Δ`, `(V·∇)W` and `𝔓` up to lower-order shifts: `T₀ΔV = Δ(T₀V) + ΔV`,
`T₀(V·∇W) = (T₀V)·∇W + V·∇(T₀W) + ½ V·∇W`, `T₀𝔓F = 𝔓T₀F`. Hence every comoving derivative
`T₀^m U` lies in `IsUniformSmoothL4SliceFamily` without any `L⁴` bound on radial drifts.

## Proved here (zero `sorry`)
* linear calculus and uniqueness of `HasComovingJetDeriv` (`ComovingTowerSub`);
* the order-`n` comoving class `ComovingTowerSub.ComovingOrder`, its closure under `+`, `•`, `-`, `Δ`,
  `(·∇)·`, `𝔓` and `comovingEvolRHS`, and the tower `m ↦ comovingDerivOf^[m] V`
  (`ComovingTowerSub.exists_comovingTower`);
* `bgComovingFirstEquation_of` (`PartII-b:S3/1/1/2/1` from `PartII-b:S3/1/1/2/1/2`,
  `PartII-b:S3/1/1/2/1/3`), `bgFirstPhaseDerivStep_of_comoving` (`PartII-b:S3/1/1/2` from
  `PartII-b:S3/1/1/2/1`), `bgHigherOrderPhaseDerivTower_of_comoving` (`PartII-b:S3/1/2` from
  `PartII-b:S3/1/2/3`, `PartII-b:S3/1/2/4`, `PartII-b:S3/1/2/5`, `PartII-b:S3/1/1/2/1` and the
  accepted `smoothLeraySliceRegularity_proof`).
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

noncomputable section

open Set MeasureTheory Filter Topology
